"of known flaws. It has never been migratable, so it is unlikely to be used "
"in any serious virtualization setting. Modern ISAs provide on-CPU "
"cryptography instructions (e.g. AES-NI/VAES, armv8 crypto extensions), and "
"the Linux kernel deprecated AF_ALG and dropped its off-CPU accelerator "
"support in Linux 7.2, removing the primary userspace path for off-CPU crypto "
"acceleration. The time for this sort of off-load has passed."
msgstr ""

